speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I wish to add a few words to the statement just made by the Minister of Finance.
When postal employees in group D are given pay increases under the continuing salary review, the only ones who do not receive an increase are those in the following categories, who are paid out of revenue and whose salary rates are established by the Postmaster General as authorized by the Post Office Act.
1.	Postmasters-Semi-staff post offices, groups 31 to 34;
2.	Assistants 1 and 2-Semi-staff post offices;
3.	Postmasters-Revenue post offices, groups 1 to 30;
4.	Postmasters-Sub post offices.
(Text):
These employees will have their salaries adjusted at the same time as those who are paid out of appropriations. The increase will be proportionate to that granted the classes paid from appropriations. The effective date will be the same as for group D.
